memfd_create and the pidfd calls without the Linux option (ADRs 0613 and
0614), as patch 0120 has inotify: the sysdep tags and signatures of
pidfd_open, pidfd_getpid and pidfd_send_signal leave the Linux option's
block, so a system layer without that option can implement them, and
memfd_create, with its MFD_ flags, leaves it too. The flags gain Linux's
MFD_NOEXEC_SEAL and MFD_EXEC. The Radix system layer builds the Linux
option's options/linux/generic/sys-pidfd.cpp and installs its
<sys/pidfd.h> (ports/mlibc/build.sh), which need nothing of Linux's and
nothing under the GPL: both files are mlibc's own, under the MIT license.

